  "limits": "One required-durable native approval task over real loopback TCP and owned SQLite. Separate fresh grant-insert and park-journal-insert precommit failures each retain committed admission and Running, disclose no interrupt/prompt/grant, close an admitted 200 SSE stream, and fault authorized pending reads with 503 host_unready. A healthy fixture observes one complete interrupt and independently committed unconsumed grant, matching park snapshot, prompt, identity, revision and journal before authorized pending disclosure; ordinary state omits the token. Hard-kill/reap followed by direct SQLite reopen preserves the same typed/raw park evidence at owner generation plus one. This does not prove arbitrary crash points, postrestart HTTP disclosure or recovery, resume, other approval modes, every TCP schedule, current-HEAD TypeScript COMPAT, M0, CP-001\u2013010, full core, or whole-product parity. T-019 through T-056 remain pending."
